T*
(Background: Acute kidney injury in critically ill populations carries substantial) Tj
T*
(morbidity and mortality. Preclinical studies suggest vitamin D metabolites possess) Tj
T*
(renoprotective and immunomodulatory properties. This protocol describes a phase 2) Tj
T*
(randomized investigation of two activated vitamin D formulations in high-risk intensive) Tj
T*
(care patients. Methods: One hundred fifty adults with critical illness and baseline kidney) Tj
T*
(dysfunction risk factors will be randomized to one of three arms: calcifediol) Tj
T*
(\(25-hydroxyvitamin D derivative\), calcitriol \(1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D derivative\), or) Tj
T*
(placebo, administered orally. Primary composite outcome combines 7-day mortality, need for) Tj
T*
(renal replacement therapy, and magnitude of serum creatinine elevation using a pre-) Tj
T*
(specified ranking procedure. Secondary outcomes include incidence of new kidney injury,) Tj
T*
(laboratory biomarkers, and transcriptomic analysis of immune cells. Safety monitoring) Tj
T*
(focuses on hypercalcemia incidence. Study design incorporates intent-to-treat analysis) Tj
T*
